Description: RAM guard that freezes the program filling the memory
 Gagarine keeps a Linux machine from freezing when its memory fills up. It
 measures the RAM every second (four times per second above 85 %). At 95 %
 it freezes (SIGSTOP) the program that grows the fastest, throttles it (if
 resumed, it can only grow by a small amount), pushes it into swap, then
 stops it if the RAM does not go down once the swap-out is done, if the RAM
 reaches 98 %, or if it stays frozen for 10 minutes.
 .
 It runs as a system service (root), never touches the desktop or critical
 services, and sends desktop notifications offering to stop or resume the
 frozen program. The "gagarine essai" command checks the whole chain safely.
 .
 It also sets up a compressed swap in RAM (zram, the size of the RAM, zstd,
 used before the disk swap) with matching kernel settings, so that frozen
 programs are pushed out fast and the machine never thrashes the disk.
 .
 It includes a queue for heavy jobs ("gagarine file"): several jobs can run
 together when the RAM and the cores allow it, ordered by priority, each one
 locked into a kernel memory limit, so a runaway job cannot take the machine
 down. The queue remembers the memory each job really used
 and corrects announcements that are too low, and it notifies on the desktop
 (and optionally on the phone through ntfy) when a job ends.
 .
 Gagarine also acts before the threshold: it freezes a program that would
 fill the RAM within seconds, or when the kernel is already stalling on
 memory pressure. It keeps a 7-day history of the RAM and of the biggest
 programs ("gagarine historique"), and cleans up idle memory hogs (Gradle and
 Kotlin daemons, models loaded in LM Studio or Ollama) with a user timer
 ("gagarine menage"). It can cap the memory of desktop applications such as
 Chrome or VS Code ("gagarine applications").
 .
 It also spots memory leaks (a program whose memory climbs steadily, or a job
 whose peak grows from one run to the next) and warns before the threshold.
 .
 A hook for Claude Code sessions ("gagarine hook-claude") refuses heavy jobs
 launched outside the queue and suggests the right command, and a status line
 ("gagarine ligne-etat") shows the state of the machine in Claude Code.
 .
 The package installs a signed APT repository entry, so "apt upgrade" keeps
 Gagarine up to date.
 .
 A GNOME graphical interface ("gagarine-interface", GTK 4 and libadwaita)
 shows the RAM, the swap, the frozen programs, the job queue, the journal
 and the settings, and drives the service. A panel indicator
 ("gagarine-indicateur") shows the RAM in the top bar at all times. Both are
 optional: they need the recommended packages.
 .
 Complements systemd-oomd and earlyoom.
